---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const schemas = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Person',
    name: 'Waqar',
    jobTitle: 'Dietitian',
    url: 'https://tdeecheck.com/about/',
    worksFor: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'TDEE Check', url: 'https://tdeecheck.com/' },
    knowsAbout: ['TDEE', 'BMR', 'Calorie planning', 'Macronutrients', 'Weight management'],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About TDEE Check - Dietitian Reviewed Calorie Calculators"
  description="About TDEE Check: free calorie, TDEE, BMR, macro, and BMI calculators built on published formulas and reviewed by Waqar, Dietitian."
  path="/about/"
  schemas={schemas}
  crumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'About', path: '/about/' },
  ]}
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pt-10">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink-900">About TDEE Check</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      TDEE Check exists for one simple reason: most people who struggle with their weight are not lacking willpower, they
      are lacking a reliable number. Advice like "eat less" is useless without knowing less than what. Our calculators turn
      your stats into clear daily calorie and macro targets, using the same published formulas that dietitians and
      researchers use, presented in plain language with no sign up and no paywall.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">Reviewed by a dietitian</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      The content and calculators on this site are reviewed by <strong>Waqar</strong>, a practicing
      <strong>Dietitian</strong>. That review means the formulas are the right ones, the safety floors are stated honestly,
      and the guidance matches what a professional would tell a client in a first session: start with a reasonable target,
      track the trend, adjust in small steps, and never chase extreme deficits. Health content on the internet is full of
      confident nonsense, so every page here names its formula and its limits.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">How we calculate</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-6">
      <li><strong>BMR:</strong> the Mifflin-St Jeor equation (1990), the best validated prediction formula for most adults, with the Katch-McArdle equation offered when body fat percentage is known.</li>
      <li><strong>TDEE:</strong> BMR multiplied by a standard activity factor from 1.2 (sedentary) to 1.9 (athlete).</li>
      <li><strong>Weight change estimates:</strong> based on the widely used approximation that one pound of body fat stores about 3,500 kcal.</li>
      <li><strong>BMI:</strong> the standard World Health Organization adult categories, always presented with context about what BMI cannot measure.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">What this site is not</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      TDEE Check is an educational tool, not a clinic. The numbers are estimates for healthy adults and are not a
      substitute for personal medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. If you have a medical condition, are pregnant or
      breastfeeding, or have a history of eating disorders, please work with your own clinician or dietitian. You can read
      the full <a class="font-bold text-brand-700 underline" href="/medical-disclaimer/">medical disclaimer</a> and reach
      us through the <a class="font-bold text-brand-700 underline" href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">Start calculating</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      New here? Run your numbers through the <a class="font-bold text-brand-700 underline" href="/">TDEE Calculator</a>,
      then explore the <a class="font-bold text-brand-700 underline" href="/calculators/">full calculator set</a> and the
      <a class="font-bold text-brand-700 underline" href="/blog/how-to-calculate-tdee/">step by step guide</a> on how the
      math works.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
